{"skill":{"slug":"slack","displayName":"Slack"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545378002,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2315,"sha256":"e15de2ab67a9ee4949c4fce1e5a2685da7eb4575096c1b10bd898499fc844eb3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1816,"sha256":"bbfd6c002129d29cadad4817ea883282852a7d3eb5c05bf195f32a39fb04deb0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013605748,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3fb592fd566fd42495c863b285303d4092debb58c912e91498f4e523dd4b60dc","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3fb592fd566fd42495c863b285303d4092debb58c912e91498f4e523dd4b60dc","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: slack\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw skill bundle for Slack is benign. The `SKILL.md` defines a set of actions (react, send/edit/delete messages, manage pins, fetch member info) that are standard for a Slack integration. It explicitly states it uses a pre-configured bot token and does not contain any instructions for data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection against the agent beyond its stated purpose of interacting with Slack.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159625148},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":8,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789013605748},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This Slack skill clearly documents Slack bot actions and does not show hidden code, installation behavior, persistence, or unrelated data handling.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of the configured Slack bot token is expected for a Slack-control skill, and the artifact does not request local filesystem, shell, browser, or unrelated environment access.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no executable scripts, dependencies, install hooks, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose message read/send/edit/delete and pin actions, but they do not add extra privacy minimization guidance for member info or explicit confirmation guidance for destructive Slack actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanisms, background workers, scheduled tasks, memory writes, privilege escalation, or tool hijacking behavior are present in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to control Slack via the Clawdbot slack tool, and the documented capabilities match that purpose: reactions, messages, pins, member info, and emoji list.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want Clawdbot to act in Slack with its configured bot permissions. Be careful with send, edit, delete, pin, and unpin actions because they can affect shared channels, and request member info only when it is needed for the task.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The memberInfo action is disclosed and consistent with Slack administration/help workflows, but the scanner's privacy-minimization concern is reasonable user guidance rather than evidence of hidden or purpose-mismatched behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013605748}}}}}